    "question": {
      ":question/id": "97a431d2-d458-5eaa-821d-d0849a9cb9f4",
      ":question/problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/generate/scratch/17592186110756-draft/plots/65af24e38742745ff5368dfb0afc548d74c7c02cf4644f637bdfdd111ea396c0.png)\n\nThe diagram above shows the unit circle. Given that the $y$-coordinate of the point $P$ is $\\frac{3\\sqrt{3}}{14},$ use the Pythagorean identity to find $sec\u2061\\theta .$",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "19625f0b-c6a0-5fb7-9d6e-2f1356271bf0",
